#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:12
msgid "Carbonate Reactions, Buffering, and pH"
msgstr "Reacciones carbonatadas, tampón y pH"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:14
msgid ""
"Carbonates provide the majority of the buffering for drinking water as long "
"as the pH is close to neutral. These equations provide a basis to calculate "
"how much base or acid must be added to a natural water to achieve a target "
"pH."
msgstr ""
"Los carbonatos proporcionan la mayor parte del tampón durante agua potable "
"siempre que el pH esté cerca del neutro. Estas ecuaciones proporcionan una "
"base para calcular cuánta base o ácido debe añadirse a un agua natural para "
"alcanzar un pH objetivo."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:20
msgid "Carbonic Acid and Bicarbonate"
msgstr "Ácido carbónico y bicarbonato"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:22
msgid ""
"{H_2}CO_3^{\\star} \\overset {K_1} \\longleftrightarrow {H^+} + HCO_3^-\n"
"\n"
msgstr "{H_2}CO_3^{\\star} \\overset {K_1} \\longleftrightarrow {H^+} + HCO_3^-"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:26
msgid "Where:"
msgstr "Donde:"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst
msgid ":math:`K_1` is the dissociation constant defined below."
msgstr ":math:`K_1` es la constante de disociación definida a continuación."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:28
msgid ""
"{K_1} = \\frac{{\\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]\\left[ {HCO_3^ - } "
"\\right]}}{{\\left[ {{H_2}CO_3^{\\star} } \\right]}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:30
msgid ""
"Where the [ ] indicates concentration in mole/L. We will use the p function,"
" :math:`p(x)=-log_{10}(x)`, to define the dissociation constant."
msgstr ""
"Donde el [ ] indica concentración en mol/L. Usaremos la función p, "
":math:`p(x)=-log_{10}(x)`, para definir la constante de disociación."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:32
msgid ""
"p{K_1} = 6.3\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:34
msgid ""
"At the point of equal concentrations of bicarbonate and carbonic acid the "
"dissociation constant, :math:`K_1`, is equal to the hydrogen ion "
"concentration, :math:`H^ +`. Thus we have equal concentrations at "
":math:`p{K_1} = pH`. This reaction is “centered” at pH = 6.3 and thus there "
"is maximum buffering due to this reaction at pH = 6.3."
msgstr ""
"En el punto de concentraciones iguales de bicarbonato y ácido carbónico, la "
"constante de disociación, :math:`K_1`, es igual a la concentración de iones "
"hidrógeno, :math:`H^ +`. Así, tenemos concentraciones iguales en "
":math:`p{K_1} = pH`. Esta reacción está \"centrada\" en pH = 6,3 y, por "
"tanto, hay un máximo tampón debido a esta reacción en pH = 6,3."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:39
msgid "Bicarbonate and Carbonate"
msgstr "Bicarbonato y carbonato"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:41
msgid ""
"HCO_3^ - \\overset {{K_2}} \\longleftrightarrow {H^ + } + CO_3^{ - 2}\n"
"\n"
msgstr "HCO_3^ - \\overset {{K_2}} \\longleftrightarrow {H^ + } + CO_3^{ - 2}"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:43
msgid ""
"{K_2} = \\frac{{\\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]\\left[ {CO_3^{ - 2}} "
"\\right]}}{{\\left[ {HCO_3^ - } \\right]}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:45
msgid ""
"p{K_2} = 10.3\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:47
msgid "Thus the carbonate system also provides buffering around pH 10.3."
msgstr ""
"Así, el sistema carbonatado también proporciona amortiguación alrededor de "
"pH 10,3."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:52
msgid "Total Concentration of Carbonates"
msgstr "Concentración total de carbonatos"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:54
msgid "The total concentration of carbonate species is given by"
msgstr "La concentración total de especies carbonatadas está dada por"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:56
msgid ""
"{C_T} = \\left[ {{H_2}CO_3^{\\star} } \\right] + \\left[ {HCO_3^ - } "
"\\right] + \\left[ {CO_3^{ - 2}} \\right]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:58
msgid "Where: :math:`{C_T}` is the total concentration of carbonates."
msgstr "Dónde: :math:`{C_T}` es la concentración total de carbonatos."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:60
msgid ""
"The total concentration of carbonates, :math:`{C_T}`, is useful because it "
"is conservative (in a closed system) even though the individual species "
"concentrations change as pH changes."
msgstr ""
"La concentración total de carbonatos, :math:`{C_T}`, es útil porque es "
"conservadora (en un sistema cerrado) aunque las concentraciones individuales"
" de especies cambien a medida que cambia el pH."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:65
msgid "Alpha Notation"
msgstr "Notación alfa"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:67
msgid ""
"The alpha notation is used to show the concentration dependence on pH and to"
" make the equations simpler."
msgstr ""
"La notación alfa se utiliza para mostrar la dependencia de la concentración "
"respecto al pH y para simplificar las ecuaciones."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:69
msgid ""
"\\left[ {{H_2}CO_3^{\\star} } \\right] = {\\alpha_0}{C_T}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:71
msgid ""
"\\left[ {HCO_3^-} \\right] = {\\alpha_1}{C_T}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:73
msgid ""
"\\left[ {CO_3^{-2}} \\right] = {\\alpha_2}{C_T}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:75
msgid ""
"The alphas sum to 1 because each :math:`\\alpha` is the fraction of the "
"carbonates corresponding to that species. The alphas are each a function of "
"the proton concentration and the dissociation constants of the carbonate "
"reactions."
msgstr ""
"Los alfas suman 1 porque cada :math:`\\alpha` es la fracción de los "
"carbonatos correspondiente a esa especie. Los alfas son función de la "
"concentración de protones y de las constantes de disociación de las "
"reacciones carbonatadas."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:77
msgid ""
"{\\alpha_{\\text{0}}} = \\frac{1}{{1 + \\frac{{{K_1}}}{{[{H^ + }]}} + "
"\\frac{{{K_1}{K_2}}}{{{{[{H^ + }]}^2}}}}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:79
msgid ""
"{\\alpha_{\\text{0}}} = \\frac{1}{{1 + \\frac{{{K_1}}}{{[{H^ + }]}}\\left( "
"{1 + \\frac{{{K_2}}}{{[{H^ + }]}}} \\right)}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:81
msgid ""
"{\\alpha_{\\text{1}}} = \\frac{1}{{\\frac{{[{{\\rm H}^ + }]}}{{{{\\rm "
"K}_1}}} + 1 + \\frac{{{{\\rm K}_2}}}{{[{{\\rm H}^ + }]}}}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:83
msgid ""
"{\\alpha_{\\text{2}}} = \\frac{1}{{\\frac{{{{[{{\\rm H}^ + }]}^2}}}{{{{\\rm "
"K}_1}{{\\rm K}_2}}} + \\frac{{[{{\\rm H}^ + }]}}{{{{\\rm K}_2}}} + 1}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:85
msgid ""
"{\\alpha_{\\text{2}}} = \\frac{1}{{1 + \\frac{{[{{\\rm H}^ + }]}}{{{{\\rm "
"K}_2}}}\\left( {1 + \\frac{{[{{\\rm H}^ + }]}}{{{{\\rm K}_1}}}} \\right)}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:90
msgid "Acid Neutralizing Capacity (ANC) or Alkalinity"
msgstr "Capacidad neutralizante de ácidos (ANC) o alcalinidad"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:92
msgid ""
"Acid neutralizing capacity or alkalinity is the ability of a water sample to"
" react with and neutralize an input of acid. The units of ANC are "
"equivalents (or protons) per liter. Bicarbonate, :math:`HCO_3^-`, can react "
"with one proton, :math:`H^+`, and thus each mole of :math:`HCO_3^-` provides"
" one equivalent per liter of ANC. The other terms in the equation have "
"similar explanations."
msgstr ""
"La capacidad neutralizante de ácidos o alcalinidad es la capacidad de una "
"muestra de agua para reaccionar y neutralizar una entrada de ácido. Las "
"unidades de ANC son equivalentes (o protones) por litro. El bicarbonato, "
":math:`HCO_3^-`, puede reaccionar con un protón, :math:`H^+`, y así cada mol"
" de :math:`HCO_3^-` proporciona un equivalente por litro de ANC. Los otros "
"términos de la ecuación tienen explicaciones similares."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:94
msgid ""
"{\\text{ANC}} = [HCO_3^ - {\\text{] + 2[CO}}_3^{ - 2}{\\text{] + "
"[O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}}{\\text{] - [}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + "
"}}}{\\text{]}}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"{\\texto{ANC}} = [HCO_3^ - {\\texto{] + 2[CO}}_3^{ - 2}{\\texto{] + "
"[O}}{{\\texto{H}}^{\\texto{ - }}}{\\texto{] - [}}{{\\texto{H}}^{\\texto{ + "
"}}}{\\texto{]}}"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:96
msgid ""
"Note that carbonic acid and dissolved carbon dioxide are not in the ANC "
"equation because they have no ability to neutralize protons."
msgstr ""
"Cabe señalar que el ácido carbónico y el dióxido de carbono disuelto no "
"están en la ecuación de ANC porque no tienen capacidad para neutralizar los "
"protones."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:98
msgid "We can write the ANC equation using alpha notation"
msgstr "Podemos escribir la ecuación ANC usando notación alfa"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:100
msgid ""
"ANC = {C_T}({\\alpha_1} + 2{\\alpha_2}) + \\frac{{{K_w}}}{{\\left[ {{H^ + }}"
" \\right]}} - \\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:104
msgid ""
"For completeness we include acid neutralizing capacity for the case where "
"the system is in equilibrium with atmospheric carbon dioxide, :math:`CO_2`."
msgstr ""
"Para mayor completitud, incluimos la capacidad neutralizadora de ácidos en "
"el caso en que el sistema esté en equilibrio con el dióxido de carbono "
"atmosférico, :math:`CO_2`."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:107
msgid ""
"ANC_{atm\\,equilibrium} = "
"\\frac{{{P{C{O_2}}}{K_H}}}{{{\\alpha_0}}}({\\alpha_1} + 2{\\alpha_2}) + "
"\\frac{{{K_w}}}{{\\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]}} - \\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:112
msgid "pH Adjustment"
msgstr "Ajuste del pH"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:114
msgid ""
"The final ANC, :math:`ANC_1`, after base addition and aluminum coagulant "
"addition is given by"
msgstr ""
"El ANC final, :math:`ANC_1`, tras la adición de bases y la adición de "
"coagulante de aluminio, se obtiene por"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:116
msgid ""
"ANC_1 = ANC_0 + \\Pi_{base}C_B + \\Pi_{Al}C_{Al}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"ANC_1 = ANC_0 + \\Pi_{base}C_B + \\Pi_{Al}C_{Al}\n"
"\n"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:118
#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:130
msgid "where:"
msgstr "donde:"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:119
msgid ":math:`ANC_0` is the initial acid neutralizing capacity of the water sample."
msgstr ""
":math:`ANC_0` es la capacidad inicial neutralizante de ácido de la muestra "
"de agua."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:120
msgid ""
":math:`ANC_1` is the final acid neutralizing capacity of the mixture after "
"the base and aluminum coagulant is added."
msgstr ""
":math:`ANC_1` es la capacidad final neutralizante de ácido de la mezcla "
"después de añadir la base y el coagulante de aluminio."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:121
msgid ":math:`C_B` is concentration of base in mole/liter"
msgstr ":math:`C_B` es la concentración de base en mol/litro"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:122
msgid ":math:`\\Pi_{base}` is ANC per mole of base"
msgstr ":math:`\\Pi_{base}` es ANC por mol de base"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:123
msgid ":math:`C_{Al}` is the concentration of coagulant in mole of aluminum/liter"
msgstr ":math:`C_{Al}` es la concentración de coagulante en el mole de aluminio/litro"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:124
msgid ":math:`\\Pi_{Al}` is ANC per mole of aluminum"
msgstr ":math:`\\Pi_{Al}` es la ANC por mol de aluminio"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:126
msgid "The final carbonate concentration is given by"
msgstr "La concentración final de carbonato está dada por"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:128
msgid ""
"C_{T_1} ={C_{T_0}}+ \\Pi_{CO_3^{-2}}C_B\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:131
msgid ""
":math:`C_{T_1}` is the final total carbonate concentration of the mixture "
"after the base is added."
msgstr ""
":math:`C_{T_1}` es la concentración total final de carbonato de la mezcla "
"tras añadir la base."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:132
msgid ""
":math:`\\Pi_{CO_3^{-2}}` is mole of carbonate per mole of base (0 for "
":math:`NaOH` and 1 for :math:`Na_2CO_3`)"
msgstr ""
":math:`\\Pi_{CO_3^{-2}}` es mole de carbonato por mol de base (0 para "
":math:`NaOH` y 1 para :math:`Na_2CO_3`)"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:134
msgid "Substituting these values into the ANC equation we obtain"
msgstr "Sustituyendo estos valores en la ecuación ANC obtenemos"

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:136
msgid ""
"ANC_0 + \\Pi_{base}C_B + \\Pi_{Al}C_{Al} = ({C_{T_0}}+ "
"\\Pi_{CO_3^{-2}}C_B)({\\alpha_1} + 2{\\alpha_2}) +  \\frac{{{K_w}}}{{\\left["
" {{H^ + }} \\right]}} - \\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:138
msgid ""
"Now we solve for :math:`C_B`, the concentration of base that must be added "
"to reach a target pH."
msgstr ""
"Ahora resolvemos para :math:`C_B`, la concentración de base que debe "
"añadirse para alcanzar un pH objetivo."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:140
msgid ""
"(\\Pi_{base} -\\Pi_{CO_3^{-2}}({\\alpha_1} + 2{\\alpha_2}) )C_B= "
"{C_{T_0}}({\\alpha_1} + 2{\\alpha_2}) +  \\frac{{{K_w}}}{{\\left[ {{H^ + }} "
"\\right]}} - \\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right] - ANC_0 - \\Pi_{Al}C_{Al}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:142
msgid ""
" C_B= \\frac{{C_{T_0}}({\\alpha_1} + 2{\\alpha_2}) +  "
"\\frac{{{K_w}}}{{\\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right]}} - \\left[ {{H^ + }} \\right] -"
" ANC_0 - \\Pi_{Al}C_{Al}}{\\Pi_{base} -\\Pi_{CO_3^{-2}}({\\alpha_1} + "
"2{\\alpha_2})}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:147
msgid ""
"Note that the equations above can also be used for the case where acid is "
"added to reduce the pH. In that case :math:`\\Pi_{base}` will have a "
"negative value."
msgstr ""
"Nótese que las ecuaciones anteriores también pueden usarse en el caso en que"
" se añade ácido para reducir el pH. En ese caso :math:`\\Pi_{base}` tendrá "
"un valor negativo."

#: ../../Chemistry_of_Water_Treatment/Chemistry_Derivations.rst:149
msgid ""
"An example using this equation to find the required amount of base addition "
"is given in :ref:`heading_Example_pH_Adjustment`."
msgstr ""
"Un ejemplo usando esta ecuación para encontrar la cantidad requerida de suma"
" de bases se da en :ref:`heading_Example_pH_Adjustment`."

